{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Compose ONE commit message for ONE store unit (lib.ctl) in a repo - READ-ONLY, stages/commits nothing. The unit's own diff is the source of truth, so the message is correct no matter WHO edited (agent, peer, MCP, or hand). Prompt = recent house-style subjects + sibling units changed in the same batch + the unit's capped diff (incl. generated rust). Enforces the contract: subject <=72 chars imperative, blank line, 1-4 why-bullets, an Agent-Message trailer naming the arm. Falls back to a deterministic mechanical message when the LLM fails or misbehaves, so the caller can always commit. Returns {message, source:\"llm\"|\"fallback\", unit}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse crate::agent::llm::ask_llm::ask_llm;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"unit","type":"String"},{"name":"siblings","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"stxkgw1a101903675m1a7c","readers":[],"time":1791027770584,"username":"system","writers":[]}